course: dictionary
lesson: 1253
title: Words that tell a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some verbs describe a crime in one word. To burgle a building means to break into it and steal things. «The neighbours were burgled while they were on holiday.» The clues are holiday and an empty house: someone got in and took things while nobody was home.
explain: Burgle is a verb, so its ending changes with the time. «Someone burgled our flat last week.» Burgled is the past, because it happened last week. Try burgles or burgling in the same sentence and check that the ending still fits the time.
explain: Words can also be made from other words. «Burgle» was made from «burglar» by chopping off the ending that looked like -ar. Edit was made the same way from editor. This is called back-formation, and it is one way new verbs appear.
explain: People in the UK and Australia usually say burgle. Americans more often say burglarize, so a book from the USA may use a different word for the same crime. Context and a dictionary will help you check.
fact: To burgle means to break into a building or home and steal things.
fact: Burgle is a verb: burgle, burgles, burgled, burgling.
fact: A burglar is the person who burgles, and burgle was made from burglar by back-formation.
fact: In UK and Australian English, burgle is the usual word; Americans more often say burglarize.
fact: Burgled is the past form: «The neighbours were burgled.»
exercise: «The neighbours were burgled while they were on holiday.» What does burgled mean? | Locked out by mistake | Painted a fence | Given a present | *Broken into and things stolen
exercise: «Someone burgled our flat last week.» Which words tell you when it happened? | our flat | *last week | burgled | someone
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a person who burgles. | *burglar | building | burgles | editor
test: Fill the gap: «Last night, thieves ___ the shop.» | burgle | burgles | burgling | *burgled
test: Burgle was made from which word by chopping off an ending? | burgling | thief | editor | *burglar
exam: Mum says, «We were burgled, so we changed all the locks.» What happened to their home? | The furniture was moved outside | Someone painted the kitchen | *Thieves broke in and stole things | They gave away their keys
